{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1504295-the-occult-skill-what-exactly-does-the-skill-do","id":1504295,"title":"The Occult SKILL : What exactly does the SKILL do?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-03T15:28:51-08:00","id":1504295,"title":"The Occult SKILL : What exactly does the SKILL do?","content":"What exactly can a character do with the Occult <b>SKILL</b>? (Not the charms).<br /> <br /> Just the skill.<br /> <br /> I remember in 2E Occult and Thauamaturgy got bloated and the Devs cut them down for 3E But there is <b><i>NOTHING in the 3E Core book about what the Occult skill does.</i></b><br /> <br /> Does it do Geomancy? Do you summon spirits? Speak with the dead? Do you summon rain?<br /> <br /> What does Occult do?<br /> <br /> What can a PC with <b>just </b>the Occult skill do?\u200b<br /> <br /> Also Regarding Thamaturgy :<br /> <br /> When I first looked around, most people were saying that 2E Thaumaturgy's functions had been folded into Occult and I thought fair enough but neither the Book OR online sources seems to give details regarding this.<br /> \u200b<br /> There is no detail for what Occult does at all and Thaumaturgy's functions are simply not present in 3E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","name":"TryingToBeSlim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T17:00:16-08:00","id":1504299,"title":"","content":"It facilitates.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, like Lore, Occult is a skill about knowing things. Even without Charms or Thaumaturgy, Occult lets you know things so you can apply your other skills in ways people without that knowledge wouldn't know to do.<br /> <br /> So it both does a lot, and nothing, at the same time, because by itself it's academic. You need other skills to put that knowledge to functional use. But without that knowledge, there's so much your character wouldn't know to try that could make huge differences in their adventures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T18:31:14-08:00","id":1504306,"title":"","content":"Thing is Lore has some rules.<br /> <br /> Occult has <b>none </b>in the core book apparently.<br /> <br /> Also does that mean what I was told about Thaumaturgy being folded into Occult was completely wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","name":"TryingToBeSlim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T20:41:16-08:00","id":1504331,"title":"","content":"There's a bit of a difference between not having an specific subsystem, and not having any rules (Bureaucracy is in a similar boat if you want to say it has &quot;no rules&quot;).<br /> <br /> As for thaumaturgy... kinda? You can't use Thaumaturgy rituals with just a rating in Occult. But if you have the Thaumaturge Merit, then you just buy rituals and use Occult, you don't have whole schools and such to invest in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T22:21:02-08:00","id":1504333,"title":"","content":"I tried fleshing Occult out by giving it the ability to make wards and function like Lore when it comes to knowing about spirits/mysticism.<br /> <br /> Otherwise there's a reason I agree with Essence merging Lore and Occult (not so much also including medicine).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-04T17:00:49-08:00","id":1504393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1504295-the-occult-skill-what-exactly-does-the-skill-do#post1504295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there is <b><i>NOTHING in the 3E Core book about what the Occult skill does.</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div>There's its description under the Abilities heading.<br /> <br /> Occult is an Ability to know what various kinds of spirits can do and what might compel and motivate them beyond their personalities as people. Things like what kind of burning branch produces a smoke that repulses or draws them, that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> It is also an Ability one can use to represent insight into things that are just plain weird about Creation. Things like inexplicable curses coming upon people, or how to recognise the chicken eggs that hatch into basilisks.<br /> <br /> It's not so much an ability for summoning spirits as it is for knowing if a given spirit is naturally inclined to be summoned and what might be assembled to do so. Like, you're not rolling it on its own to do so, you're doing it to know if a given variety of god can sense papyrus inscribed with a given poem being burned on the night of the waning crescent moon and coming before you in good humour.<br /> <br /> There might be some places in the world where such actions can affect the weather, but not across the board, and not with a fully fleshed out system for how it works.<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy represents being an individual with an innate uncanny capacity for bringing up certain preternatural occurrences. Ultimately, the Occult Ability comes out more as knowing such people than being them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-04T19:15:20-08:00","id":1504403,"title":"","content":"So is it possible for mortals to use a line of salt to block ghosts without needing to be born with a miracle/mutation Merit?<br /> What happened to knowing the escape conditions for Neomah and beckoning one?<br /> What about looking at the stars and recognizing constellations and planets? Do mortals need the Thaumaturgy mutation Merit to know what the constellations are?<br /> <br /> Is all this knowledge now inherently inborn in only a few rare mutant people, and can't be taught or passed down? That's the thing about the Merit, it's presented as this inexplicable <i>thing</i> that only a tiny number of people anywhere have, and it can't be taught. And each &quot;ritual&quot; is basically a Charm that only one mutant has ever had access to. I don't understand how &quot;pour a line of salt&quot; is something that mortals can't teach or learn. &quot;Cry over a stillborn baby&quot; shouldn't be hard to undetstand, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-04-2023, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T06:25:50-08:00","id":1504418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1504295-the-occult-skill-what-exactly-does-the-skill-do?p=1504403#post1504403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is it possible for mortals to use a line of salt to block ghosts without needing to be born with a miracle/mutation Merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes; this is an innate weakness of that being. Honestly, Second Edition making that into a thaumaturgy ritual was actually making it more restrictive than it made any sense to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happened to knowing the escape conditions for Neomah and beckoning one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I'm unsure if that detail of demons is still intended to be present, as such conditions have not been referenced in any write-ups that I can find. Still, that's another thing where I feel as though thaumaturgy overrode the actual steps and just wound up as highly specialized miniature sorcery. If it <i>is</i> possible for neomah to come forth when menstrual blood mixes with freshly wept tears, a ritual one spent XP on should hardly be necessary to know that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about looking at the stars and recognizing constellations and planets? Do mortals need the Thaumaturgy mutation Merit to know what the constellations are?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, mortal understanding of the Constellations is actually referenced in Charting Fate's Course.<br /> <br /> Basically, people often have an understanding of what the Constellations mean that aligns with the symbolism by which they inform the powers of Sidereals, but many cultures attribute their own meanings to them, that may or may not be related to the Sidereal ones. People often regard the placement of the stars as auspicious or otherwise, but that's not so much prediction of the future as people letting such things inform the timing of when they'll do something on the assumption that it will be blessed or cursed. The movements of the stars are not said to directly reflect influences in the Loom of Fate, but they can have a certain ephemeral connection to things happening in the world connected to their purviews.<br /> <br /> That is to say that being born under the sign of the Lovers doesn't strictly say anything about Heaven's plans for your life, but the meaning of that sign might inform how you live more often than not.<br /> <br /> But for the most part, people's relationship with the stars is much like it has tended to be in real life. An actual, genuine power to foresee the future is indeed a function of the Thaumaturgist Merit, which can take the form of examining the night sky and people's personal star charts as surely as it does examining tea leaves or drawing cards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is all this knowledge now inherently inborn in only a few rare mutant people, and can't be taught or passed down? That's the thing about the Merit, it's presented as this inexplicable <i>thing</i> that only a tiny number of people anywhere have, and it can't be taught. And each &quot;ritual&quot; is basically a Charm that only one mutant has ever had access to.</div> </div> </div> </div>A few things. First of all, not only are the example thaumaturgy rituals not supposed to be always something that only one person has ever known, the ones written up in the corebook describe how frequent they tend to be. It's said that in a society with important regional tea culture, about one person in ten thousand will possess the power to actually divine the future from tea leaves. It's only sometimes that a trick would be truly unique to an individual <i>unless they share it with other thaumaturgists</i>.<br /> <br /> Because the other thing about them is that while every thaumaturgist starts out with one particular trick, being like that means that you can learn other powers so long as you get taught directly by a thaumaturgist who knows them. Sijan is described as a place that gathers those who can use thaumaturgy, where regardless of what they started out with they can learn the funereal powers of that city.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T07:03:58-08:00","id":1504422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1504295-the-occult-skill-what-exactly-does-the-skill-do?p=1504418#post1504418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes; this is an innate weakness of that being. Honestly, Second Edition making that into a thaumaturgy ritual was actually making it more restrictive than it made any sense to be.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'm unsure if that detail of demons is still intended to be present, as such conditions have not been referenced in any write-ups that I can find. Still, that's another thing where I feel as though thaumaturgy overrode the actual steps and just wound up as highly specialized miniature sorcery. If it <i>is</i> possible for neomah to come forth when menstrual blood mixes with freshly wept tears, a ritual one spent XP on should hardly be necessary to know that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes more sense. Really, the salt ward thing ought to be common knowledge, especially in Sijan and Chiaroscuro. Knowing how to beckon a single kind of First Circle demon shouldn't take many Occult dots. And unless Games of Divinity is retconned, even a mortal queen can accidentally give Ligier an opening to escape Malfeas, if he wants to right then. Many of the escape conditions struck me as things mortals would cause accidentally in a lot of cases. You just killed and ate the last dodo... now here's a blood ape to eat <i>you</i>!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1504295-the-occult-skill-what-exactly-does-the-skill-do?p=1504418#post1504418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The movements of the stars are not said to directly reflect influences in the Loom of Fate, but they can have a certain ephemeral connection to things happening in the world connected to their purviews.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the idea of them being a &quot;display screen for the Loom&quot; is kinda gone? Or totally gone? That makes it more reasonable for typical mortals to be unable to use it profitably. It also clears up something that confused me: the constellations would presumably be stationary, more so than threads in the Loom. So you'd need a whole lot of wandering stars/comets flitting among constellations to display the Loom's activity, even vaguely. 5 planets plus Luna would not be enough, beyond things like horoscopes.<br /> <br /> The part about Sijan confused me because it talked about teaching rituals where the rest talked about them being un-teachable. You can't write them down, so... words just fail to describe them? It isn't made concrete how they are taught at all. I guess it's meant to imply they have to be demonstrated instead of described in words, and only another thaumaturge can understand what they witnessed?<br /> <br /> One of my difficulties with thaumaturgy as a Merit is the idea that it's like a mutation. In the 1E Player's Guide, thaumaturgy was just humans clumsily fiddling with the universal laws of fate. Anybody could do it, but most Dragon Kings didn't bother. It wasn't presented as special unique human magic. I like a rare innate talent for <i>learning</i> rituals like conjuring a flame, or exorcism... but not all of them. Any humans being born with magic nobody else gets, or magic they know without being taught, counters the idea that mortals have no innate magic at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T07:53:18-08:00","id":1504425,"title":"","content":"Well, considering anything capable of learning Sorcery (which is still generally Exalted, but potentially other Essence users) gets the Merit for free? I think it comes off more that &quot;some humans manage to luck into a bit of supernatural power that's above their station,&quot; than it does, &quot;this is a uniquely human form of magic.&quot; A human might be born with Exalted Healing, but that doesn't really make a grand statement about humanity in the setting.<br /> <br /> A lot of this is also going to be hard to address because we don't have a book on spirits and demons yet; and some of the metaphysics as presented in 3e have changed a bit from 2e. 3e's full write up of how demons work (whatever book that's in) might include ways demons can enter Creation without being summoned, and thus how any mortal with Occult could at least try to unlock the door even if they can't actively make a demon go through it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T08:08:03-08:00","id":1504427,"title":"","content":"IIRC sorcerous initiation grants the Merit but mere potential for sorcery doesn't.<br /> <br /> It does remain to be seen whether Dragon Kings or Jadeborn can have that Merit, or get it for free, or are locked out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T09:03:54-08:00","id":1504433,"title":"","content":"Yeah, poorly worded on my part. You need to actually get Sorcery before you get the Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T10:13:24-08:00","id":1504451,"title":"","content":"The description of the Thaumaturgist merit specifies that it's only Exalted who get that benefit. Mortals would have to buy both at full cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T10:25:25-08:00","id":1504456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1504295-the-occult-skill-what-exactly-does-the-skill-do?p=1504422#post1504422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes more sense. Really, the salt ward thing ought to be common knowledge, especially in Sijan and Chiaroscuro. Knowing how to beckon a single kind of First Circle demon shouldn't take many Occult dots. And unless Games of Divinity is retconned, even a mortal queen can accidentally give Ligier an opening to escape Malfeas, if he wants to right then. Many of the escape conditions struck me as things mortals would cause accidentally in a lot of cases. You just killed and ate the last dodo... now here's a blood ape to eat <i>you</i>!</div> </div> </div> </div>Checking back, I find I was mistaken; in Hundred Devils Night Parade, the write-up for Rimvidas the Cancerous Cornucopia states that they can be drawn unbidden into Creation by desperate prayers for change whispered into a moonless night, and the Third Circle Demon Sibri, the Rampart of Serpents, might enter the world to answer the prayers of slaves, the abused, and princes under the yoke of a greater power (as well as generally favouring outcasts, children and the elderly, and the impoverished, maimed, or chronically ill). <br /> <br /> That said, I would still think that often the knowledge of what calls demons is a bit obscure, regarded as perilous even by those who know it, and more often such conditions are fulfilled spontaneously and in a more sincere fashion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also clears up something that confused me: the constellations would presumably be stationary, more so than threads in the Loom. So you'd need a whole lot of wandering stars/comets flitting among constellations to display the Loom's activity, even vaguely. 5 planets plus Luna would not be enough, beyond things like horoscopes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always assumed that the stars of Creation had positions fixed relative to one another, but that the night sky would shift over time in a manner resembling looking up from the surface of a rotating spheroid. The planets would still be distinguished by moving about within this tableau in a manner that creates numerous permutations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The part about Sijan confused me because it talked about teaching rituals where the rest talked about them being un-teachable. You can't write them down, so... words just fail to describe them? It isn't made concrete how they are taught at all. I guess it's meant to imply they have to be demonstrated instead of described in words, and only another thaumaturge can understand what they witnessed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would take it as one part being a complex thing that is highly based in the experience in a manner that is difficult to put into words, one part a form of tacit knowledge, and one part there being something innately obscure and uncanny about it that can only be passed on by a personal interchange.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my difficulties with thaumaturgy as a Merit is the idea that it's like a mutation. In the 1E Player's Guide, thaumaturgy was just humans clumsily fiddling with the universal laws of fate. Anybody could do it, but most Dragon Kings didn't bother. It wasn't presented as special unique human magic. I like a rare innate talent for <i>learning</i> rituals like conjuring a flame, or exorcism... but not all of them. Any humans being born with magic nobody else gets, or magic they know without being taught, counters the idea that mortals have no innate magic at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the element where mortal humans are distinguished can still be found in the point that the vast <i>vast</i> majority of them have no such powers, contrasted with my presumption that every Dragon King has at least a few. I like to think of that as often making them a bit of a fresh canvas upon which the uncanny and the weird can leave its impressions, and as far as thaumaturgy goes that extends to the very nature of the world itself, big elemental flat earth that it is, floating tentatively on a sea of chaos. The small oddities are dotted around enough that you can find a person who slips into them all over even if they're a diamond in the rough, compared to extremely obscure things like a martial arts school carrying a blessing from a patron snake god that passes to whomever is sifu, an individual with a black fire fuelled by hatred left in their heart by a Deathlord, or a man endowed with comet powers as he reassembles the fragments of a stone that fell from the sky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T13:22:50-08:00","id":1504483,"title":"","content":"I kept <i>meaning</i> to do a Storytellers Vault product on updating the less outre 1e/2e uses of thaumaturgy as 3e uses of Occult. I should dig up those notes at some point.and actually do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T16:10:32-08:00","id":1504509,"title":"","content":"Lots of good replies.<br /> <br /> Will try to address as many as I can.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> : Just double-checked Beuracracy. In all honesty I do wish it had it's own system or at least an idea of how and where to use it. What difficuulties etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1504295-the-occult-skill-what-exactly-does-the-skill-do?p=1504393#post1504393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's its description under the Abilities heading.<br /> <br /> Occult is an Ability to know what various kinds of spirits can do and what might compel and motivate them beyond their personalities as people. Things like what kind of burning branch produces a smoke that repulses or draws them, that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> It is also an Ability one can use to represent insight into things that are just plain weird about Creation. Things like inexplicable curses coming upon people, or how to recognise the chicken eggs that hatch into basilisks.<br /> <br /> It's not so much an ability for summoning spirits as it is for knowing if a given spirit is naturally inclined to be summoned and what might be assembled to do so. Like, you're not rolling it on its own to do so, you're doing it to know if a given variety of god can sense papyrus inscribed with a given poem being burned on the night of the waning crescent moon and coming before you in good humour.<br /> <br /> There might be some places in the world where such actions can affect the weather, but not across the board, and not with a fully fleshed out system for how it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is how is this any way different from LORE ?<br /> <br /> Because if Occult is only knowledge without actual use, then it really should just be a lore specialty and done. On the other hand if it does have actual use, then there should be a system or examples of how to use it.<br /> <br /> For example take Medicine. If Medicine was only knowledge then it should just be Lore (Medicine) and done. Yet Medicine is the actual ability to practice medicine. To perform medical procedures, set broken bones etc..<br /> <br /> What can a person with the Occult skill do? Can they appease/banish spirits? You mentioned weather-working should not exactly have a system but it's been described as one of the abilities mortal miracle workers possess (see pg 578)<br /> <br /> <i>Everyday Wonders<br /> Mortal miracle-workers practice <b>alchemy, geomancy, astrology, warding, weatherworking</b> and other crafts, and they\u2019ve also found ways to create drugs and charms that contain some degree of power.\u200b</i><br /> <br /> Either those Everyday Wonders (tailsmans, miracle-tea, etc) are made by Thaumaturgists and not actually every-day (or there are a LOT more thaumaturgists then the core describes) or they are made/accomplished by mortal occultists in which case the occult skill should reflect this.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","name":"TryingToBeSlim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T12:59:17-08:00","id":1504776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1504295-the-occult-skill-what-exactly-does-the-skill-do?p=1504509#post1504509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is how is this any way different from LORE ?<br /> <br /> Because if Occult is only knowledge without actual use, then it really should just be a lore specialty and done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Admittedly, Exalted is in an odd position in that its Attributes and Abilities aren't just their own thing, they're things for Exalted Charms to be hung off of, and I think there's credibility to a point that there are Charms that go under Occult as its own thing that wouldn't quite fit under the umbrella of Lore (or would at least make such a Lore feel like it covered a few very divergent elements).<br /> <br /> Still, on its own I think it's a question of what one wants the experience of interacting with Creation's supernatural oddities to be like; if it's a matter of applying information or something more intuitive and immersive and surreal, where a person needs to follow chains of certain strange logic to understand what works when. I think about something like It, where it was depicted as necessary to go on a vision quest to commune with a cosmic turtle in order to learn how to fight against the scary shapeshifter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">there should be a system or examples of how to use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ideally there would be, but there's only so much word count available in the core and something like new Lore rules probably had to take priority.<br /> <br /> I think it's also a matter of how the things Occult engages with often don't have system intricacy in their own right the way that something like a disease does so that the substance of a successful roll comes down to changing a level of intensity or a duration or something. I feel as though most of the time it's going to come down to advancing the plot.<br /> <br /> That said, many entries of Hundred Devils Night Parade refer to what Occult can be used to know about or navigate or harness them.<br /> <br /> Still, I don't think I said it was just about knowledge, I believe I made points there to the effect that it can provoke responses from entities and circumstances that are appropriate. In cases like that, I would think it would be depicted as having the capacity to carry out the actions that bring such responses, the knack for or practice in them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What can a person with the Occult skill do? Can they appease/banish spirits? You mentioned weather-working should not exactly have a system but it's been described as one of the abilities mortal miracle workers possess (see pg 578)</div> </div> </div> </div>If it should not exactly have a system then it should inexactly have one. The little corner of the setting in which one places their game has a hill in which carrying out the correct rituals will affect the weather. Generally it's a difficulty 3 or 4 action. It makes whatever weather condition was called for that more or less affects an appropriate region surrounding the hill. It does not have the precision of something like lowering intensity levels equal to threshold successes.<br /> <br /> <i>Everyday Wonders<br /> Mortal miracle-workers practice <b>alchemy, geomancy, astrology, warding, weatherworking</b> and other crafts, and they\u2019ve also found ways to create drugs and charms that contain some degree of power.\u200b</i><br /> <br /> Either those Everyday Wonders (tailsmans, miracle-tea, etc) are made by Thaumaturgists and not actually every-day (or there are a LOT more thaumaturgists then the core describes) or they are made/accomplished by mortal occultists in which case the occult skill should reflect this.<br /> <br /> [/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> I think that list covers a spectrum, and you're reading the use of the term &quot;everyday&quot; there a bit too literally. I think for some parts of the list it's more about stuff that is considered mundane relative to the power of gods and Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T13:33:43-08:00","id":1504779,"title":"","content":"I would like to know whether contraception has gone from generally available worldwide to women who do not want to be pregnant every year, allowing women to be adventurers, to a miracle that only 20 people in the world can conjure from nowhere.<br /> <br /> My 3E pdf freezes Adobe or crashes <i>every time</i> I try to use the search function, or just searches for <i>every effing word that starts with m</i>, so this is not easy to simply look up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Edit: I managed to find the &quot;everyday wonders&quot; that only &quot;miracle-workers&quot; (thaumaturges) can create. So &quot;widely available&quot; maiden tea is apparently something only the super-rare miracle-workers can make. That makes no sense!<br /> <br /> Boiling some herb should not be that hard. I boil leaves in a pot all the time. It's easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-07-2023, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T13:55:02-08:00","id":1504780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1504295-the-occult-skill-what-exactly-does-the-skill-do?p=1504779#post1504779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I managed to find the &quot;everyday wonders&quot; that only &quot;miracle-workers&quot; (thaumaturges) can create.</div> </div> </div> </div>When it says mortal miracle workers there, I feel as though it's somewhere between &quot;thaumaturge&quot; and &quot;person whom others would refer to that way in a hyperbolic affectionate sense&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for maiden tea, it's as the book describes, coming in a few grades with varying levels of efficacy; the most reliable one is composed of the rarest ingredients and goes at a high price.<br /> <br /> I think that on the whole, maiden tea is... far better contraception than people have had through most of human history, possibly a bit less reliable than commonly used modern prophylactics in their most affordable form, and have the all-around benefit of not needing to be something that has to be wrapped around or inserted into the body (albeit with significant risks if one messes up the dosage).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T16:12:24-08:00","id":1504789,"title":"","content":"I hope you're right about the &quot;miracle-workers&quot; in that section, otherwise it contradicts itself.<br /> <br /> Thankfully there are bookmarks, I found the Abilities descriptions. Under the War vignette, <i>&quot;everyone knew what salt did to undead flesh\u2026\u200b&quot;</i> so the salt ward thing, at least, is common knowledge. Under War instead of Occult, which maybe suggests it doesn't require <i>any</i> particular Ability (Which is what I would assume, unless you live in a culture where such knowledge has been deliberately hidden or mortals are trained to reflexively let monks and Exalted think about all such things for them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-07-2023, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T03:17:27-07:00","id":1505300,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7JCHAxW2KEI&amp;t=8s\" target=\"_blank\">Here's your answer.</a><br /> <br /> I mean technically you can use it as &quot;lore, but for magic stuff&quot; but that's strictly redundant with Lore unless you deliberately lop off all supernatural knowledge from it - normally Lore covers <i>academic</i> knowledge of many fields, while Occult is <i>applied</i> knowledge, but in 3e there is no such thing as applied Occult without unique special powers.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1504295-the-occult-skill-what-exactly-does-the-skill-do?p=1504393#post1504393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Occult is an Ability to know what various kinds of spirits can do and what might compel and motivate them beyond their personalities as people. Things like what kind of burning branch produces a smoke that repulses or draws them, that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> It is also an Ability one can use to represent insight into things that are just plain weird about Creation. Things like inexplicable curses coming upon people, or how to recognise the chicken eggs that hatch into basilisks.<br /> <br /> It's not so much an ability for summoning spirits as it is for knowing if a given spirit is naturally inclined to be summoned and what might be assembled to do so. Like, you're not rolling it on its own to do so, you're doing it to know if a given variety of god can sense papyrus inscribed with a given poem being burned on the night of the waning crescent moon and coming before you in good humour.<br /> <br /> There might be some places in the world where such actions can affect the weather, but not across the board, and not with a fully fleshed out system for how it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are all also Lore, though. Unless you want to argue that as soon as something becomes too &quot;supernatural&quot; it vanishes from Lore, which doesn't make any sense - why would a learned sage's knowledge of a region and its inhabitants suddenly stop dead when it comes to spirits? Or, at least, require that they have twice as much effort to learn it?<br /> <br /> The divide causes problems. Suppose I was a learned sage who wanted to give a lecture on the following things:<br /> <br /> 1. The <i>false</i> (purely cultural or apocryphal in nature) supernatural beliefs, histories, and entities of a particular region. None of the things in this lecture are real; they're just folk-lore. This plainly isn't occult (because it has nothing to do with actual spirits), so it's Lore.<br /> <br /> 2. Supernatural beliefs, histories, and entities of a particular region <i>that have actually valid foundations</i>. Now this is lecture depends on Occult?<br /> <br /> What if I'm unsure whether a particular bit of ancient lore is reliable or not?<br /> <br /> Is knowledge of historical weather patterns Lore or Occult? What about knowledge of the capabilities of different types of Exalted and their histories? If I wanted to know something obscure about the powers of various Exigents that have appeared, is that Lore or Occult? What if I want to know something obscure about the powers of various <i>spirits</i>?<br /> <br /> Creation is a magical setting, so pretty much all of Lore is going to be, to some extent or another, magical in nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T10:54:52-07:00","id":1505333,"title":"","content":"I thought of something: wouldn't it make sense for Sidereals to automatically gain access to divination &quot;rituals&quot; (like tea leaf reading and reading the stars) for free with their Second Breath?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-15T11:25:00-07:00","id":1505443,"title":"","content":"Well, it's not entirely 'free', but Seer's Starry Eye (Occult 3, Essence 1) basically does that for any Sidereal who wants to go heavy into Thaumaturgy from the start. They get the Astrology reskin of Reading the Tea Leaves and can pick up 4 more dots worth from an appropriate teacher for no XP, and more if they feel like repurchasing it later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26730-tomdick-harry","name":"TomDick&Harry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T17:25:19-07:00","id":1506190,"title":"","content":"Thanks.<br /> <br /> So even Sidereals need a Charm to look at the stars and be able to see what planet is in which constellation? If that's what it says, that's crappy.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1504295-the-occult-skill-what-exactly-does-the-skill-do?p=1504418#post1504418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, mortal understanding of the Constellations is actually referenced in Charting Fate's Course.<br /> <br /> Basically, people often have an understanding of what the Constellations mean that aligns with the symbolism by which they inform the powers of Sidereals, but many cultures attribute their own meanings to them, that may or may not be related to the Sidereal ones. People often regard the placement of the stars as auspicious or otherwise, but that's not so much prediction of the future as people letting such things inform the timing of when they'll do something on the assumption that it will be blessed or cursed. The movements of the stars are not said to directly reflect influences in the Loom of Fate, but they can have a certain ephemeral connection to things happening in the world connected to their purviews.<br /> <br /> That is to say that being born under the sign of the Lovers doesn't strictly say anything about Heaven's plans for your life, but the meaning of that sign might inform how you live more often than not.<br /> <br /> But for the most part, people's relationship with the stars is much like it has tended to be in real life. An actual, genuine power to foresee the future is indeed a function of the Thaumaturgist Merit, which can take the form of examining the night sky and people's personal star charts as surely as it does examining tea leaves or drawing cards.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is bothering me on a reread of the thread. IIRC they made it so that no accurate information at all can come from the stars without magic mutations, and all astrology is nothing but silly superstitions or squinting at actually invisible things. I hope I'm misunderstanding.<br /> <br /> <b>Any</b> human being can look at the stars IRL and see where the constellations, moon, and visible planets are. You don't need a telescope to see Mercury, Venus, Mars, Jupiter, or Saturn, let alone some weird mutation. You just need to go somewhere without modern electric light pollution, which doesn't exist in Creation anyway.<br /> <br /> It makes sense that the stars do not display details in the current state of the Loom of Fate or future events. But if Jupiter is ascending in the Gull while Mars is descending in the Corpse on a night of the waning half moon, that means something for what's auspicious or inauspicious right this minute, or for someone born right this minute. That meaning is actually objectively real. A culture may have lost all accurate knowledge of the stars, but there's no way it takes a weird mutation to be able to just see Jupiter. The visible planets, by definition, ain't invisible. They even have colors!<br /> <br /> It's like... a genetic test at birth can detect that a baby has cystic fibrosis, OK. Most people don't have DNA tests on hand or use them on every baby. People may try to predict babies' future with superstitions that don't work, but their genes are still real and influence their life even if nobody knows the technique to read them. Superstition isn't the only possible way to interact with inborn disease.<br /> <br /> Being born under the Lovers isn't as detailed as your DNA but it still matters more than stars in real life, even if everyone in your country mistakenly thinks you were born under the Dancing Bear instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-22-2023, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T18:54:36-07:00","id":1506198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1504295-the-occult-skill-what-exactly-does-the-skill-do?p=1505300#post1505300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Creation is a magical setting, so pretty much all of Lore is going to be, to some extent or another, magical in nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is like saying that an understanding of electron transitions between atomic energy levels is practically relevant to an understanding of dog behaviour.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1504295-the-occult-skill-what-exactly-does-the-skill-do?p=1506190#post1506190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks.<br /> <br /> So even Sidereals need a Charm to look at the stars and be able to see what planet is in which constellation? If that's what it says, that's crappy.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone can look at the sky, only some people can tell the future from it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is bothering me on a reread of the thread. IIRC they made it so that no accurate information at all can come from the stars without magic mutations, and all astrology is nothing but silly superstitions</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not think these books intend to look so derisively on the cultures contained within its setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes sense that the stars do not display details in the current state of the Loom of Fate or future events. But if Jupiter is ascending in the Gull while Mars is descending in the Corpse on a night of the waning half moon, that means something for what's auspicious or inauspicious right this minute, or for someone born right this minute. That meaning is actually objectively real.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I'm putting it together, if a person's life displays characteristics that seem to suggest a particular consistent pattern that corresponds with some of the mystical significance of the arrangement of stars at the time of their birth, then there is a connection between those things, but the majority of people born under those circumstances will not actually have any impact on them from it (even if some societies will think they do).<br /> <br /> Apart from everything else, I think the alternative would produce a bit of an odd setting; thousands of people are born simultaneously all the time, does one want a setting where large numbers of the population all have such a significant common influence on who they are as people?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T23:22:28-07:00","id":1506216,"title":"","content":"I've always been disappointed with what Occult allows characters to do. So I allow players to use Occult to do magic stuff. It's a fantasy world and I keep it to mostly folklore kind of magic... small rituals and spells kinda stuff, and I'm very clear to players that the effects they get from Charms will be much more powerful, much less Sorcery. But I show Occult being used by mortals this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T02:17:02-07:00","id":1506218,"title":"","content":"Occult is fairly oddly specific and, in my opinion, a little anaemic. Something I noticed in 'Exalted Essence' is that it defines thaumaturges differently from the corebook, calling it out as exploiting occult mechanisms in the world through Sagacity rather than having some intrinsic X factor that allows you to do it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Many are the mortal miracle workers practicing alchemy, geomancy, astrology, warding, weather working, and other crafts. Most often, these minor miracles exploit hidden occult mechanisms in Creation placed by the gods or Exalted of yore, accessed by using the Sagacity Skill via rituals of lesser magic called thaumaturgy. While some thaumaturges ply an honest trade, cold readers and conniving would-be soothsayers out to defraud a mark outnumber them.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> It then goes on to list various Everyday Wonders. In ExEss terms it's Sagacity which is a combination of Lore/Occult/Medicine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T14:05:14-07:00","id":1506359,"title":"","content":"For me, Occult in Exalted (and WoD, actually) functions like WoD Politics. Your Politics rating is not a measure how how much you <i>know about</i> politics, it's how well you <i>do</i> politics. How well-connected you are, what offices you hold etc.<br /> <br /> In an Occult context, this feels more like applied knowledge. If you want to know about demons, that's Lore. If you want to actually summon one and do it well, that's Occult. It folds some practical knowledge into the thing, but the ability to perform tasks is the core of the Ability for me. Yes, you may need other things as well, but Occult reflects things like technique be as well, which binary things like &quot;is/is not a sorcerer or thaumaturge&quot; cannot do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T20:31:44-07:00","id":1506599,"title":"","content":"I use a homebrew version of Thaumaturgy from 1E and 2E, with the score in Occult contributing to the number of Arts/Sciences and their ranking (apprentice, initiate, adept, master) that the character has learned. I was very disappointed with the 3E direction for Thaumaturgy, but that is just my personal preference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26886-lindharin","name":"Lindharin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T20:10:41-07:00","id":1506701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lindharin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1504295-the-occult-skill-what-exactly-does-the-skill-do?p=1506599#post1506599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I use a homebrew version of Thaumaturgy from 1E and 2E, with the score in Occult contributing to the number of Arts/Sciences and their ranking (apprentice, initiate, adept, master) that the character has learned. I was very disappointed with the 3E direction for Thaumaturgy, but that is just my personal preference.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've more or less done the same thing. I took a number of Thaumaturgy rituals or concepts from the earlier editions and turned Occult into a sort of &quot;Craft&quot; skill, insofar as it's about crafting purely magical items. For example, if you want to make alchemical healing elixers, that will be under traditional Craft. But under Occult you could create talismans that can provide minor blessings, or cause hinderances. Creating appropriate salt barriers to keep out ghosts would be an Occult roll. Occult is also used for performing magical rituals (such as prayers to a spirit to provide blessings or cursing one's enemies).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T12:55:41-07:00","id":1507068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lindharin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1504295-the-occult-skill-what-exactly-does-the-skill-do?p=1506599#post1506599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I use a homebrew version of Thaumaturgy from 1E and 2E, with the score in Occult contributing to the number of Arts/Sciences and their ranking (apprentice, initiate, adept, master) that the character has learned. I was very disappointed with the 3E direction for Thaumaturgy, but that is just my personal preference.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1504295-the-occult-skill-what-exactly-does-the-skill-do?p=1506701#post1506701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've more or less done the same thing. I took a number of Thaumaturgy rituals or concepts from the earlier editions and turned Occult into a sort of &quot;Craft&quot; skill, insofar as it's about crafting purely magical items. For example, if you want to make alchemical healing elixers, that will be under traditional Craft. But under Occult you could create talismans that can provide minor blessings, or cause hinderances. Creating appropriate salt barriers to keep out ghosts would be an Occult roll. Occult is also used for performing magical rituals (such as prayers to a spirit to provide blessings or cursing one's enemies).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWould either of you mind sharing your systems? Please? *gives puppy-dragon stare*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","name":"TryingToBeSlim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T13:38:30-07:00","id":1507076,"title":"","content":"Mine wouldn't actually be helpful, since I'm not using the Exalted (or Essence) systems. I have a homebrew Cortex game going on, and I converted my favorite concepts from 1E and 2E Thaumaturgy to use Cortex rules. I'd recommend checking out the Exalted Player's Guide from 1st Edition, and the Book Of Sorcery 3 Oadenol's Codex from 2nd Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26886-lindharin","name":"Lindharin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}